# CLASSICAL-PERSISTENCE-ONLY
# Exercises `actor {} <: Principal` across an actor-class upgrade: a stable var
# typed `actor {}` in v0 migrates into a `Principal`-typed var in v1.
#
# Classical re-serialises the stable record through Candid (stabilize/destabilize),
# so the old `service`-encoded value reads back as a `principal` — the representation
# coincides, so it round-trips. EOP is DELIBERATELY excluded for now: it gates the
# upgrade with the RTS `memory_compatible` check (idl.rs, a Candid-subtyping checker
# over the serialized type table), which lacks a `service <: principal` case and traps
# with "Memory-incompatible program upgrade". Enable EOP once that rule lands (in
# lockstep with the Candid spec extension) — see the PR discussion / plan item 3.
install $ID actor-sub-principal-stable/version0.mo ""
ingress $ID show "DIDL\x00\x00"
upgrade $ID actor-sub-principal-stable/version1.mo ""
ingress $ID show "DIDL\x00\x00"
